{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 756150,
  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44116626",
      "title": "Configuring & Using SSG",
      "lectureOrder": 326,
      "videoOrder": 308,
      "sourceHash": "32b8f197d83bb0900759912cab83c51b29a392128ceef4c37258d2737c05de90",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.51,
          "end": 1.92,
          "en": "To add pre-rendering",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 1.92,
          "end": 5.64,
          "en": "to an Angular application, you need to run that same command",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.64,
          "end": 8.767,
          "en": "you ran before to add server-side rendering,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.767,
          "end": 13.173,
          "en": "@angular/ssr must be added with the ng add command.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.43,
          "end": 17.31,
          "en": "So here in this project, I did already run that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.31,
          "end": 19.92,
          "en": "so nothing needs to be done here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.92,
          "end": 22.08,
          "en": "This is all already prepared.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.08,
          "end": 24.21,
          "en": "Because pre-rendering, in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.21,
          "end": 28.98,
          "en": "is just a sub form of server-side rendering, you could say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 28.98,
          "end": 32.4,
          "en": "especially since you might not want to pre-render",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 32.4,
          "end": 36.27,
          "en": "all your routes, the ones that rely on data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 36.27,
          "end": 39.24,
          "en": "that must be as up to date as possible",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 39.24,
          "end": 42.06,
          "en": "can't be pre-rendered, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 42.06,
          "end": 45.93,
          "en": "But out of the box when building an Angular application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 45.93,
          "end": 50.82,
          "en": "and enabling server-side rendering, Angular will already try",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 50.82,
          "end": 53.55,
          "en": "to pre-render some pages.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 53.55,
          "end": 57.24,
          "en": "And you can see that in the Angular JSON configuration file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 57.24,
          "end": 61.26,
          "en": "There, you should find a pre-render option, which is set",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 61.26,
          "end": 66.09,
          "en": "to true out of the box, which means Angular tries",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 66.09,
          "end": 69.753,
          "en": "to identify pages that can be pre-rendered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 70.74,
          "end": 73.74,
          "en": "And by default, it identifies pages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 73.74,
          "end": 77.01,
          "en": "as pre-renderable if they're not dynamic,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 77.01,
          "end": 80.463,
          "en": "which means if they don't have dynamic route parameters.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 81.72,
          "end": 83.07,
          "en": "So in this application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 83.07,
          "end": 87.3,
          "en": "all those user-related pages would not be pre-rendered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 87.3,
          "end": 91.2,
          "en": "because they have this dynamic user ID parameter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 91.2,
          "end": 95.49000000000001,
          "en": "and Angular doesn't know in advance which user IDs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 95.49000000000001,
          "end": 97.71000000000001,
          "en": "you have in your application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 97.71000000000001,
          "end": 100.68,
          "en": "So it can't pre-render all those different pages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 100.68,
          "end": 102.333,
          "en": "for the different users.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 103.83,
          "end": 106.53,
          "en": "But it, for example, can pre-render",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 106.53,
          "end": 109.113,
          "en": "this no task component page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 110.16,
          "end": 112.65,
          "en": "and it indeed did so.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 112.65,
          "end": 115.03,
          "en": "If you take a look in your dist folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 115.95,
          "end": 117.93299999999999,
          "en": "after running npm run build,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 118.95,
          "end": 122.01,
          "en": "and there you take a look at the browser folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 122.01,
          "end": 127.01,
          "en": "you will see that in there in the index HTML file here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 127.59,
          "end": 130.83,
          "en": "which is the starting page HTML file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 130.83,
          "end": 135.12,
          "en": "In there, you will actually see that content",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 135.12,
          "end": 137.91,
          "en": "from that no task component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 137.91,
          "end": 141.27,
          "en": "this fallback text that you should select a user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 141.27,
          "end": 142.63,
          "en": "to see their tasks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 143.64,
          "end": 147.15,
          "en": "and that list of users that was rendered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 147.15,
          "end": 152.15,
          "en": "And that is all in this file because it was pre-rendered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 152.34,
          "end": 156.42000000000002,
          "en": "Now, of course, you might want to pre-render more pages.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 156.42000000000002,
          "end": 160.44,
          "en": "You might know in advance which user IDs exist",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 160.44,
          "end": 165.39,
          "en": "and you might want to pre-render the pages for those users.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 165.39,
          "end": 168.03,
          "en": "And it turns out that you can do that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 168.03,
          "end": 171.81,
          "en": "because what you can do is you can add a new file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 171.81,
          "end": 175.32999999999998,
          "en": "to your Angular project, to the root project folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 177.137,
          "end": 178.2,
          "en": "for example, and give that any file name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 178.2,
          "end": 183.09,
          "en": "of your choice, like user-routes.txt.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 183.09,
          "end": 185.673,
          "en": "But again, the file name is up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 186.63,
          "end": 188.49,
          "en": "But it's a plain text file here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 188.49,
          "end": 192.81,
          "en": "because in this file you should now specify all the routes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 192.81,
          "end": 195.27,
          "en": "you want Angular to pre-render",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 195.27,
          "end": 199.05,
          "en": "with one route path per line.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 199.05,
          "end": 202.983,
          "en": "So for example, users/u1/tasks,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 204.03,
          "end": 208.89,
          "en": "and users/U2/tasks, and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 208.89,
          "end": 211.29,
          "en": "So these now must be valid paths",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 211.29,
          "end": 213.72,
          "en": "that would work in your application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 213.72,
          "end": 215.85,
          "en": "And if that's the case, you can go back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 215.85,
          "end": 218.4,
          "en": "to the Angular JSON file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 218.4,
          "end": 221.64,
          "en": "and change this pre-render setting from true",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 221.64,
          "end": 224.46,
          "en": "to an object, which allows you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 224.46,
          "end": 227.463,
          "en": "to configure pre rendering in greater detail.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 228.36,
          "end": 230.91,
          "en": "Because here in this object, you can now add",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 230.91,
          "end": 234.1,
          "en": "a routes file property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 235.17000000000002,
          "end": 237.99,
          "en": "and set this to the path to the file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 237.99,
          "end": 241.26,
          "en": "that contains the routes that should be pre-rendered,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 241.26,
          "end": 245.13,
          "en": "in my case, user-routes.txt.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 245.13,
          "end": 247.8,
          "en": "So this is a path seen relative",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 247.8,
          "end": 250.68,
          "en": "from the root project folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 250.68,
          "end": 253.83,
          "en": "If you do that, and you save this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 253.83,
          "end": 256.023,
          "en": "and you run npm Run build again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 257.19,
          "end": 261.03,
          "en": "you will see that as the build process runs here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 261.03,
          "end": 263.34,
          "en": "more routes are pre-rendered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 263.34,
          "end": 266.94,
          "en": "Here, Angular tells me that three different static routes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 266.94,
          "end": 268.323,
          "en": "were pre-rendered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 269.79,
          "end": 272.13,
          "en": "and if we go to the dist routing folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 272.13,
          "end": 274.32,
          "en": "into the browser folder, we can now see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 274.32,
          "end": 278.34000000000003,
          "en": "that users folder with the U1 and U2 sub folders",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 278.34000000000003,
          "end": 280.68,
          "en": "with the tasks sub folders",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 280.68,
          "end": 283.77,
          "en": "and their respective index HTML files,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 283.77,
          "end": 285.45,
          "en": "which contain the content",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 285.45,
          "end": 289.383,
          "en": "for these specific users, like their name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 290.79,
          "end": 295.74,
          "en": "So now Angular did execute the components that were required",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 295.74,
          "end": 298.68,
          "en": "for these paths during the build process",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 298.68,
          "end": 300.99,
          "en": "and it pre-rendered those pages.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 300.99,
          "end": 303.06,
          "en": "And as mentioned, if you pre-render",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 303.06,
          "end": 305.22,
          "en": "all your applications pages,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 305.22,
          "end": 308.13,
          "en": "you could just deploy this browser folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 308.13,
          "end": 310.5,
          "en": "and you would have a static web app again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 310.5,
          "end": 312.6,
          "en": "which consists of multiple pages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 312.6,
          "end": 315.543,
          "en": "that have all been pre-rendered at build time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 316.5,
          "end": 320.31,
          "en": "Alternatively, you deploy both browser and server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 320.31,
          "end": 323.28,
          "en": "and you therefore have a mixture of pre-rendered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 323.28,
          "end": 325.95,
          "en": "and dynamically rendered pages.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 325.95,
          "end": 329.1,
          "en": "And that's the effort is third option you have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 329.1,
          "end": 332.133,
          "en": "when it comes to building Angular application.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
